ompatibility commitment, and the options available to\napplication teams (Angular Material, Optimus UI, or any other\nlibrary).\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs: address review feedback on migration plan page\n\n- Note that the migration plan is current and subject to change\n- Add FAQ entry on retaining PrimeNG helpers for Optimus UI\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: markuczy <markuczy@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqloEuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAh9UQAKtkgKoUBCiJcKUHYmg9vToB\nI+J2BB/giUVs6cSPt846+dgkNIivshfoJE8UdpxTS7qsWFygJ65RYDvf0zlSN/m6\n4mSIBXk0pOXXd4fWIXruVCj80CQUMd8GNQRrSXQSgEbzUHwRh3kmyzgxu4biU8dq\nH+Tl8IsIGsB1yd3aF+48KzHV0gXu4p0Y/EhbEJFNojDw6T+cMaTj8wppUgEq61dl\nv4VEjwS45MhukZxmK39R2lBbFeekJjF42WpYLINLzehZraL28H/nqfDxhb/T3U84\novSLJWwekJZtKDtMRD71fY+tov9FqnIWN8bftl0ZKGL1faV815ArWtHR2Tkmqhgl\n/azNb1qMG/T2xV/421KyR1cn6+eY7Mv+ifaukaBJjhZZoVOcqITStYFICFFMb8kw\nAhOfpWonKWWBA9bxORvPaWTaHvVTzPAdwBFiNblyG8VT7EXS9rR+1T2lKe/C3XKg\nIMEcI2lpcdTM+vYCJ3HLz8IYru1jm0LdXe7oI8lK2YQ3jElvbHmFrWdqL92ht1D3\n3DDfa9373iEgAhmmhagkpuMdZsPgoZpwNPvYr8b4jAd3MqLiC079Wi/DtB6qCIE6\n6s14m2nbAUoOqnnb4fkkVpHBCwmrrOJxNAYFk1KSjYwDUheMIXzFltRwzHHPYOda\nWBGGPZhSlAOWDSv5ikIn\n=Qowl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T07:39:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/onecx/onecx-portal-ui-libs/commit/0acb0b4e9a0cba8948e167d626d4f66218c4b098","node_id":"C_kwDOKg2NxNoAKDBhY2IwYjRlOWEwY2JhODk0OGUxNjdkNjI2ZDRmNjYyMThjNGIwOTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/onecx/onecx-portal-ui-libs/commit/ff4f65def6d437755f6049bafa676cfe3ac112a0","sha":"ff4f65def6d437755f6049bafa676cfe3ac112a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/onecx/onecx-portal-ui-libs/commits/ff4f65def6d437755f6049bafa676cfe3ac112a0"}],"sha":"0acb0b4e9a0cba8948e167d626d4f66218c4b098","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/onecx/onecx-portal-ui-libs/commits/0acb0b4e9a0cba8948e167d626d4f66218c4b098"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/129275100?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markuczy/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markuczy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markuczy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markuczy/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/markuczy","id":129275100,"login":"markuczy","node_id":"U_kgDOB7SU3A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markuczy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markuczy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markuczy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markuczy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markuczy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/markuczy","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/onecx/onecx-portal-ui-libs/commits/ff4f65def6d437755f6049bafa676cfe3ac112a0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T07:26:49Z","email":"129275100+markuczy@users.noreply.github.com","name":"markuczy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T07:26:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: implement issue #524 - Add per-button severity support to dialog buttons (#1665)\n\n* fix: implement issue #524 - Add per-button severity support to dialog buttons\n\nImplements #524\n\n* fix: implement issue #524 - Add per-button severity support to dialog buttons\n\nImplements #524\n\n* test: add missing custom button severity test for all PrimeNG severities\n\nImplements the test case for custom buttons with all PrimeNG severity values,\ncompleting the test coverage for issue #524. Mirrors the pattern already used\nfor primary and secondary button severity tests.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: correct DialogButtonSeverity type to match PrimeNG - use ''warn'' not ''warning''\n\nFixes build, test, and lint failures in angular-accelerator library by:\n- Changing DialogButtonSeverity type union from ''warning'' to ''warn'' to match PrimeNG''s actual ButtonSeverity type\n- Updating PButtonDirectiveHarness test harness to correctly map ''p-button-warn'' CSS class to ''warn'' severity value\n- Updating dialog-footer component test cases to use ''warn'' instead of ''warning'' in severity arrays\n- Updating documentation to reflect the correct PrimeNG severity value\n\nImplements internal-tasks#524\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: markuczy <markuczy@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"266fb94b0993fba23b5e69fc147c1849e00f834d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/onecx/onecx-portal-ui-libs/git/trees/266fb94b0993fba23b5e69fc147c1849e00f834d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/onecx/onecx-portal-ui-libs/git/commits/ff4f65def6d437755f6049bafa676cfe3ac112a0","verification":{"payload":"tree 266fb94b0993fba23b5e69fc147c1849e00f834d\nparent 75ed5bd7a5ece8bcf05dfefd326c4255dd967173\nauthor markuczy <129275100+markuczy@users.noreply.github.com> 1788161209 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788161209 +0200\n\nfeat: implement issue #524 - Add per-button severity support to dialog buttons (#1665)\n\n* fix: implement issue #524 - Add per-button severity support to dialog buttons\n\nImplements #524\n\n* fix: implement issue #524 - Add per-button severity support to dialog buttons\n\nImplements #524\n\n* test: add missing custom button severity test for all PrimeNG severities\n\nImplements the test case for custom buttons with all PrimeNG severity values,\ncompleting the test coverage for issue #524. Mirrors the pattern already used\nfor primary and secondary button severity tests.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: correct DialogButtonSeverity type to match PrimeNG - use ''warn'' not ''warning''\n\nFixes build, test, and lint failures in angular-accelerator library by:\n- Changing DialogButtonSeverity type union from ''warning'' to ''warn'' to match PrimeNG''s actual ButtonSeverity type\n- Updating PButtonDirectiveHarness test harness to correctly map ''p-button-warn'' CSS class to ''warn'' severity value\n- Updating dialog-footer component test cases to use ''warn'' instead of ''warning'' in severity arrays\n- Updating documentation to reflect the correct PrimeNG severity value\n\nImplements internal-tasks#524\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: markuczy <markuczy@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAA