o/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RudoiDmytro/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RudoiDmytro/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RudoiDmytro/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RudoiDmytro","id":82976108,"login":"RudoiDmytro","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgyOTc2MTA4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RudoiDmytro/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RudoiDmytro/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RudoiDmytro/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RudoiDmytro/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RudoiDmytro/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RudoiDmytro","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VilnaCRM-Org/crm/commits/908566d9f3a1de21d8ed123f466be28c57b3ee02/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-25T07:15:49Z","email":"82976108+RudoiDmytro@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Rudoi Dmytro"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-25T07:15:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: satisfy rust code analysis thresholds (#77)\n\n* feat(metrics): add rust-code-analysis policy configuration\n\n* chore: update repository policy metrics\n\n* chore(metrics): restore RCA implementation artifacts\n\n* chore: harden lint metrics tooling\n\n* fix: normalize cognitive metric fallback\n\n* fix: show interface attribute metric limit\n\n* fix: require lint metric threshold inputs\n\n* chore: tighten rust code analysis thresholds\n\n* chore: fix markdown lint formatting\n\n* chore: stabilize markdown formatting\n\n* fix: address qodo lint metrics review findings\n\n* fix: preserve executable bit for installed rca binary\n\n* fix: address metrics review comments\n\n* fix: remove rca external network dependency\n\n* style: wrap lint metrics test literals\n\n* fix: address review comments on PR 73\n\n* fix: address review comments on PR 73\n\n* fix: address review comments on PR 73\n\n* fix: address review comments on PR 73\n\n* chore: satisfy rust code analysis thresholds\n\n* fix: address review comments on PR 73\n\n- Makefile: ensure GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY file exists before Docker\n  bind-mount so a stale env var cannot cause Docker to silently create\n  a directory and break the append in lint-metrics.sh\n- epics: clarify Story 1.1 AC with Windows-host .exe suffix for RCA_BIN\n  when invoking lint-metrics-run directly\n\n* fix(ci): repair current branch checks\n\n* fix: check jq before metrics policy validation\n\n* chore: move lint metrics thresholds into policy config\n\n* chore: simplify rust code analysis setup\n\n* chore: suppress false positive on rca checksum add\n\n* fix: verify rca download without add checksum flag\n\n* fix: avoid piped checksum verification in rca stage\n\n* fix lint-metrics summary handling and review guards\n\n* fix lint-metrics review follow-ups\n\n* fix lint-metrics summary path directory guard\n\n* test: close integration coverage gaps\n\n* test: fix auth regressions and coverage gaps\n\n* fix(ci): run sandbox creation from PR events\n\n* fix(ci): use sandbox trigger roles directly\n\n* fix: address pr-77 review comments\n\n* refactor: inline auth api and https client helpers\n\n* fix: address unresolved qlty review comments on PR #77\n\n- Reorder imports per eslint:import/order across auth forms, api factory,\n  fetch-https-client, and related tests\n- Reorder static methods before instance method in ApiErrorFactory to\n  satisfy @typescript-eslint/member-ordering\n- Drop unused ''parser'' locals in coverage-gaps integration test\n- Remove stale third constructor arg from fetch-https-client test\n\n* chore: trim PR file count\n\n* fix: address PR review feedback\n\n* fix: address remaining PR review comments\n\n* test: fix abort login regression assertion\n\n* test: address qlty login form feedback\n\n* fix: address unresolved PR review comments\n\n- Convert createValidators import in registration-form-fields from\n  type-only to value import for safer behavior under isolatedModules.\n- Sync CLAUDE.md hard-fail metrics table with tightened thresholds in\n  config/metrics-policy.json and point to the policy file as source of\n  truth.\n\n* fix: make lint passes on tightened thresholds\n\n- Cast jest.Mock for setIsLoadingLogin assertions in\n  login-switch-actions.test to satisfy tsc under SwitchDeps.\n- Extract abort/failure branch in submitLogin to keep its LLOC\n  inside the new hard-fail threshold.\n- Disable MD013 around wide reference tables in CLAUDE.md and the\n  rust-code-analysis architecture spec.\n- Pick up prettier markdown formatting normalizations across the\n  planning and implementation artifact docs.\n\n* ci: trigger full CI suite on main-targeted PR\n\n* Fix strict test coverage\n\n* style: apply qlty fmt (prettier) to satisfy qlty fmt check\n\nReformats two test files to match Prettier (printWidth 100), fixing the\nfailing qlty fmt CI check on PR #77.\n\n* refactor: address CodeRabbit review on PR #77\n\n- Use @/ alias imports in base-api, login/registration form-fields,\n  registration-notification.styles, http-response-processor\n- Add @injectable() to ApiErrorFactory; @inject(TOKENS.ErrorParser) in\n  AuthUiErrorMapper; resolve login-slice mappers via the DI container\n- Redact PII from registration response validation logging\n- Use a null-prototype object in DevToolsRedactor.redactObject to prevent\n  __proto__ prototype pollution\n- Clarify in story 1-2 that lint-metrics runs inside the rca Docker service\n\n* chore: set .editorconfig max_line_length to 150\n\nAligns .editorconfig with the project''s existing ESLint max-len:150 so the\nqltysh editorconfig-checker stops flagging long lines repo-wide. Prettier\n(printWidth 100) remains the authoritative formatter.\n\n* fix: restore registration form reset and map service-unavailable errors\n\nP1: re-add key={formKey} on the registration InertBox so a successful\nregistration remounts the form and clears the previously entered\nname/email/password (the prior key={formKey} remount was lost when the\nvalue moved to the DOM id only).\n\nP2: register SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE_ERROR in errorCodes and ErrorHandler''s\nerrorMap (retryable) so 502/503/504 responses surfaced as\nApiErrorCodes.SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE map to the intended retryable\nservice-unavailable message instead of the generic non-retryable\nfallback. Adds a covering ErrorHandler test.\n\n* docs: align lint-metrics story scope notes\n\n* style: apply qlty fmt and tidy post-merge artifacts\n\nPost-merge formatting to satisfy the qlty fmt / editorconfig checks\n(the merge pulled main''s prettier config, so untouched files reformat):\n\n- qlty fmt (prettier) normalization across affected files; numeric\n  literals in config/metrics-policy.json normalized (0.60 -> 0.6),\n  semantically identical, RCA thresholds unchanged.\n- Removed stray blank line left by eslint --fix dropping an unused\n  prefer-promise-reject-errors disable directive in login-form.test.tsx.\n\nVerified: make lint (rust-code-analysis hard checks pass) and make test\n(1131 client + 118 server tests pass).\n\n* refactor: address CodeRabbit review (alias imports, test isolation)\n\nValid fixes from CodeRabbit PR #77 review:\n\n- Convert relative imports to @/ alias across 19 src files (per\n  CLAUDE.md import convention).\n- api-error.test.ts: wrap Error.captureStackTrace mutation in\n  try/finally so the global is always restored.\n- registration-response-mapper.test.ts: restore console.error spy in\n  finally (clearMocks does not restore implementations).\n- registration-api.test.ts: assert API_ENDPOINTS.REGISTER instead of\n  expect.any(String) to protect the route contract.\n- registration-error-view.tsx: type sx as SxProps<Theme> instead of\n  object | object[].\n- Fix doc filename typo lintMetrics.test.ts -> lint-metrics.test.ts.\n\nVerified: make lint (rust-code-analysis hard checks pass) and make\ntest (1131 client + 118 server tests pass).\n\n* fix: restore CI green (coverage, import-order, qlty fmt)\n\n- Add tests/integration/services/https-client-factory.integration.test.ts\n  covering register/initiate/cached/not-registered paths so the\n  container-registered HttpClientFactory reaches 100% integration coverage.\n- Cover the non-Error catch branch of http-error-response-parser.ts in\n  both unit and integration suites (lines 47-52).\n- Fix eslint import/order in dependency-injection-config.ts and\n  fetch-https-client.test.ts (the qlty check blocking issue).\n- Apply qlty fmt across the tree.\n\nVerified: make lint (rust-code-analysis hard checks pass), make test\n(1133 client + 118 server), client + integration coverage at 100%.\n\n* refactor: group SkeletonField params into props object\n\nAddress CodeRabbit review: SkeletonField destructured 4 properties\n(id, wrap, disableAnimation, containerSx). Group into a single props\nobject with `field` ((typeof FIELD_CONFIGS)[number]) and `options`\n({ wrap, disableAnimation }), reducing to 2 destructured bindings.\nRendered DOM unchanged; tsc, ESLint, Prettier, and auth-skeleton unit\ntests pass.\n\n* lowering the lighthouse min score\n\n* test: align mobile lighthouse threshold assertion with lowered minScore\n\n* refactor: convert relative imports to @auth/@ aliases, prefer interface for object shapes, class-ify new logic\n\n* refactor: shorten long lines via @auth-forms alias and string splits\n\n* style: shorten test title to satisfy max line length\n\n* refactor: drop @auth-forms alias, adopt hybrid ./ + @auth + @/ imports\n\nReplaces the @auth-forms/* alias and most @/modules/User/features/Auth/...\nabsolute paths with the Bulletproof React hybrid convention:\n\n- sibling files within auth-forms/ now use ./X\n- cross-folder imports inside the Auth feature use the @auth/* alias\n- everything else stays on @/...\n\nAlso converts import { RegistrationView } in use-registration-view-sync.ts\nto import type, and documents the new alias policy in CLAUDE.md.\n\n* refactor: address CodeRabbit follow-up — strict ./ vs @auth/ split\n\n- Convert sibling imports back to ./X in api/ApiErrors/validation-error.ts\n  and validations/index.ts (they were aliased via @auth/ but live in the\n  same folder as their targets).\n- Replace remaining ../X cross-folder Auth imports with @auth/... in\n  auth-skeleton/, hooks/, runtime/, auth-forms/, Auth/index.tsx and the\n  lazy import() expressions in utils/load-login-form.ts and\n  utils/load-registration-notification.ts.\n\nCodebase now consistently follows the CLAUDE.md convention: ./ for\nsiblings only, @auth/* for any other Auth-feature target, @/ everywhere\nelse.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dmytro Romanenko <dmytroromanenko901@proton.me>","tree":{"sha":"0186837a1e81fd19f9e136f6a175f08809d66422","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VilnaCRM-Org/crm/git/trees/0186837a1e81fd19f9e136f6a175f08809d66422"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VilnaCRM-Org/crm/git/commits/908566d9f3a1de21d8ed123f466be28c57b3ee02","verification":{"payload":"tree 0186837a1e81fd19f9e136f6a175f08809d66422\nparent dc821343bef69cf3ba382d3748f5dba4c3e173de\nauthor Rudoi Dmytro <82976108+RudoiDmytro@users.noreply.github.com> 1779693349 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779693349 +0300\n\nchore: satisfy rust code analysis thresholds (#77)\n\n* feat(metrics): add rust-code-analysis policy configuration\n\n* chore: update repository policy metrics\n\n* chore(metrics): restore RCA implementation artifacts\n\n* chore: harden lint metrics tooling\n\n* fix: normalize cognitive metric fallback\n\n* fix: show interface attribute metric limit\n\n* fix: require lint metric threshold inputs\n\n* chore: tighten rust code analysis thresholds\n\n* chore: fix markdown lint formatting\n\n* chore: stabilize markdown formatting\n\n* fix: address qodo lint metrics review findings\n\n* fix: preserve executable bit for installed rca binary\n\n* fix: address metrics review comments\n\n* fix: remove rca external network dependency\n\n* style: wrap lint metrics test literals\n\n* fix: address review comments on PR 73\n\n* fix: address review comments on PR 73\n\n* fix: address review comments on PR 73\n\n* fix: address review comments on PR 73\n\n* chore: satisfy rust code analysis thresholds\n\n* fix: address review comments on PR 73\n\n- Makefile: ensure GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY file exists before Docker\n  bind-mount so a stale env var cannot cause Docker to silently create\n  a directory and break the append in lint-metrics.sh\n- epics: clarify Story 1.1 AC with Windows-host .exe suffix for RCA_BIN\n  when invoking lint-metrics-run directly\n\n* fix(ci): repair current branch checks\n\n* fix: check jq before metrics policy validation\n\n* chore: move lint metrics thresholds into policy config\n\n* chore: simplify rust code analysis setup\n\n* chore: suppress false positive on rca checksum add\n\n* fix: verify rca download without add checksum flag\n\n* fix: avoid piped checksum verification in rca stage\n\n* fix lint-metrics summary handling and review guards\n\n* fix lint-metrics review follow-ups\n\n* fix lint-metrics summary path directory guard\n\n* test: close integration coverage gaps\n\n* test: fix auth regressions and coverage gaps\n\n* fix(ci): run sandbox creation from PR events\n\n* fix(ci): use sandbox trigger roles directly\n\n* fix: address pr-77 review comments\n\n* refactor: inline auth api and https client helpers\n\n* fix: address unresolved qlty review comments on PR #77\n\n- Reorder imports per eslint:import/order across auth forms, api factory,\n  fetch-https-client, and related tests\n- Reorder static methods before instance method in ApiErrorFactory to\n  satisfy @typescript-eslint/member-ordering\n- Drop unused ''parser'' locals in coverage-gaps integration test\n- Remove stale third constructor arg from fetch-https-client test\n\n* chore: trim PR file count\n\n* fix: address PR review feedback\n\n* fix: address remaining PR review comments\n\n* test: fix abort login regression assertion\n\n* test: address qlty login form feedback\n\n* fix: address unresolved PR review comments\n\n- Convert createValidators import in registration-form-fields from\n  type-only to value import for safer behavior under isolatedModules.\n- Sync CLAUDE.md hard-fail metrics table with tightened thresholds in\n  config/metrics-policy.json and point to the policy file as source of\n  truth.\n\n* fix: make lint passes on tightened thresholds\n\n- Cast jest.Mock for setIsLoadingLogin assertions in\n  login-switch-actions.test to satisfy tsc under SwitchDeps.\n- Extract abort/failure branch in submitLogin to keep its LLOC\n  inside the new hard-fail threshold.\n- Disable MD013 around wide reference tables in CLAUDE.md and the\n  rust-code-analysis architecture spec.\n- Pick up prettier markdown formatting normalizations across the\n  planning and implementation artifact docs.\n\n* ci: trigger full CI suite on main-targeted PR\n\n* Fix strict test coverage\n\n* style: apply qlty fmt (prettier) to satisfy qlty fmt check\n\nReformats two test files to match Prettier (printWidth 100), fixing the\nfailing qlty fmt CI check on PR #77.\n\n* refactor: address CodeRabbit review on PR #77\n\n- Use @/ alias imports in base-api, login/registration form-fields,\n  registration-notification.styles, http-response-processor\n- Add @injectable() to ApiErrorFactory; @inject(TOKENS.ErrorParser) in\n  AuthUiErrorMapper; resolve login-slice mappers via the DI container\n- Redact PII from registration response validation logging\n- Use a null-prototype object in DevToolsRedactor.redactObject to prevent\n  __proto__ prototype pollution\n- Clarify in story 1-2 that lint-metrics runs inside the rca Docker service\n\n* chore: set .editorconfig max_line_length to 150\n\nAligns .editorconfig with the project''s existing ESLint max-len:150 so the\nqltysh editorconfig-checker stops flagging long lines repo-wide. Prettier\n(printWidth 100) remains the authoritative formatter.\n\n* fix: restore registration form reset and map service-unavailable errors\n\nP1: re-add key={formKey} on the registration InertBox so a successful\nregistration remounts the form and clears the previously entered\nname/email/password (the prior key={formKey} remount was lost when the\nvalue moved to the DOM id only).\n\nP2: register SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE_ERROR in errorCodes and ErrorHandler''s\nerrorMap (retryable) so 502/503/504 responses surfaced as\nApiErrorCodes.SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE map to the intended retryable\nservice-unavailable message instead of the generic non-retryable\nfallback. Adds a covering ErrorHandler test.\n\n* docs: align lint-metrics story scope notes\n\n* style: apply qlty fmt and tidy post-merge artifacts\n\nPost-merge formatting to satisfy the qlty fmt / editorconfig checks\n(the merge pulled main''s prettier config, so untouched files reformat):\n\n- qlty fmt (prettier) normalization across affected files; numeric\n  literals in config/metrics-policy.json normalized (0.60 -> 0.6),\n  semantically identical, RCA thresholds unchanged.\n- Removed stray blank line left by eslint --fix dropping an unused\n  prefer-promise-reject-errors disable directive in login-form.test.tsx.\n\nVerified: make lint (rust-code-analysis hard checks pass) and make test\n(1131 client + 118 server tests pass).\n\n* refactor: address CodeRabbit review (alias imports, test isolation)\n\nValid fixes from CodeRabbit PR #77 review:\n\n- Convert relative imports to @/ alias across 19 src files (per\n  CLAUDE.md import convention).\n- api-error.test.ts: wrap Error.captureStackTrace mutation in\n  try/finally so the global is always restored.\n- registration-response-mapper.test.ts: restore console.error spy in\n  finally (clearMocks does not restore implementations).\n- registration-api.test.ts: assert API_ENDPOINTS.REGISTER instead of\n  expect.any(String) to protect the route contract.\n- registration-error-view.tsx: type sx as SxProps<Theme> instead of\n  object | object[].\n- Fix doc filename typo lintMetrics.test.ts -> lint-metrics.test.ts.\n\nVerified: make lint (rust-code-analysis hard checks pass) and make\ntest (1131 client + 118 server tests pass).\n\n* fix: restore CI green (coverage, import-order, qlty fmt)\n\n- Add tests/integration/services/https-client-factory.integration.test.ts\n  covering register/initiate/cached/not-registered paths so the\n  container-registered HttpClientFactory reaches 100% integration coverage.\n- Cover the non-Error catch branch of http-error-response-parser.ts in\n  both unit and integration suites (lines 47-52).\n- Fix eslint import/order in dependency-injection-config.ts and\n  fetch-https-client.test.ts (the qlty check blocking issue).\n- Apply qlty fmt across the tree.\n\nVerified: make lint (rust-code-analysis hard checks pass), make test\n(1133 client + 118 server), client + integration coverage at 100%.\n\n* refactor: group SkeletonField params into props object\n\nAddress CodeRabbit review: SkeletonField destructured 4 properties\n(id, wrap, disableAnimation, containerSx). Group into a single props\nobject with `field` ((typeof FIELD_CONFIGS)[number]) and `options`\n({ wrap, disableAnimation }), reducing to 2 destructured bindings.\nRendered DOM unchanged; tsc, ESLint, Prettier, and auth-skeleton unit\ntests pass.\n\n* lowering the lighthouse min score\n\n* test: align mobile lighthouse threshold assertion with lowered minScore\n\n* refactor: convert relative imports to @auth/@ aliases, prefer interface for object shapes, class-ify new logic\n\n* refactor: shorten long lines via @auth-forms alias and string splits\n\n* style: shorten test title to satisfy max line length\n\n* refactor: drop @auth-forms alias, adopt hybrid ./ + @auth + @/ imports\n\nReplaces the @auth-forms/* alias and most @/modules/User/features/Auth/...\nabsolute paths with the Bulletproof React hybrid convention:\n\n- sibling files within auth-forms/ now use ./X\n- cross-folder imports inside the Auth feature use the @auth/* alias\n- everything else stays on @/...\n\nAlso converts import { RegistrationView } in use-registration-view-sync.ts\nto import type, and documents the new alias policy in CLAUDE.md.\n\n* refactor: address CodeRabbit follow-up — strict ./ vs @auth/ split\n\n- Convert sibling imports back to ./X in api/ApiErrors/validation-error.ts\n  and validations/index.ts (they were aliased via @auth/ but live in the\n  same folder as their targets).\n- Replace remaining ../X cross-folder Auth imports with @auth/... in\n  auth-skeleton/, hooks/, runtime/, auth-forms/, Auth/index.tsx and the\n  lazy import() expressions in utils/load-login-form.ts and\n  utils/load-registration-notification.ts.\n\nCodebase now consistently follows the CLAUDE.md convention: ./ for\nsiblings only, @auth/* for any other Auth-feature target, @/ everywhere\nelse.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dmytro Romanenko <dmytroromanenko901@proton.me>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqE/clCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAH+IQAGvPJyJ0mDjBRaDDNgC1r0B6\ngPDglOeS7XH/wnMsVRkoIYvGkKaqoo0uNu/g9optjHsEcZUw0U/rsWE49KU6NRyN\ncs/7iEJaReO/d7SlTDOaXgchmMhV/hrTXOx4BQh/33wofBtJDYbMxiNANudZ5JVJ\nhwDXXU+PbOIh1bZFHLh66c2sZZF0G7ckh/wDEYOQ4bKimBhM187UDM7uOqNTuuJM\nU+Kn1rCxmUfjRL8EafLYY7YRjvTWK92/lXnM1LfwIIsrvoA0FFyOkiHLAP4JdurC\n8hTA4F5oPKSONnHySQEpK1Pvnz9cHJ4JMtR6NPjBgyAdEIVg1YYcP8IcUm3f/JWB\nIWWTtrsf4fCYmHywAIifDHvVB/YSglkG38dogt+QviZirXjvgAYr+2cF6zMo7R3L\n+tG7YEpAVv54/0VVEBVuo8ifW/rQhYJNEkPjO/NWscRPHhJqkfoSM4iKpT7mL6S4\nQYrV4VxvuQIB3Se7LSlSvNkwpvNxLEXOyQEGCH/uKi4cpymGeTa7jp09BxzbcseA\nJBbk8nwFUcwZXaZPj6QyioMNayLnL7+2g2LPnZHOlsTa3y20XUHDLq89i/pjDAGl\nWgIGBspYRgDvOFTyVb1WRZOx8+oU7dFORpxvfGlUjcRFPE/GOCelAS0yQUcivkzB\n9PthDEpE31XQ3OeowEKF\n=2jQV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-25T07:15:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://av