/renovate","id":29139614,"login":"renovate[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90MjkxMzk2MTQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/runtime-env/runtime-env/commits/c8561f2ed687b3834fe75960416d167eecd3c072/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T00:00:40Z","email":"29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"renovate[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T00:00:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(deps): update dependency webpack to v5.111.1 (#984)\n\nThis PR contains the following updates:\n\n| Package | Change |\n[Age](https://docs.renovatebot.com/merge-confidence/) |\n[Confidence](https://docs.renovatebot.com/merge-confidence/) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [webpack](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack) | [`5.111.0` →\n`5.111.1`](https://renovatebot.com/diffs/npm/webpack/5.111.0/5.111.1) |\n![age](https://developer.mend.io/api/mc/badges/age/npm/webpack/5.111.1?slim=true)\n|\n![confidence](https://developer.mend.io/api/mc/badges/confidence/npm/webpack/5.111.0/5.111.1?slim=true)\n|\n\n---\n\n### Release Notes\n\n<details>\n<summary>webpack/webpack (webpack)</summary>\n\n###\n[`v5.111.1`](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/blob/HEAD/CHANGELOG.md#51111)\n\n[Compare\nSource](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/compare/v5.111.0...v5.111.1)\n\n##### Patch Changes\n\n- Throw on a write to an imported binding without losing concatenation.\n(by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22141](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22141))\n\n- Keep the `</html>` a page was written with, whatever opened the\nelement. (by\n[@&#8203;aryanraj45](https://redirect.github.com/aryanraj45) in\n[#&#8203;22103](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22103))\n\n- Look an attribute up by what its value decodes to, not how it was\nspelled. (by\n[@&#8203;aryanraj45](https://redirect.github.com/aryanraj45) in\n[#&#8203;22107](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22107))\n\n- Minify HTML by what a value says rather than how it was spelled. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22154](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22154))\n\n- Follow HTML template form and frameset rules during tree construction.\n(by [@&#8203;dependabot](https://redirect.github.com/apps/dependabot) in\n[#&#8203;22129](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22129))\n\n- Keep the whitespace `calc()` needs around `+` and `-` in a custom\nproperty. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22150](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22150))\n\n- Keep an attribute''s delimiter and spell its value back where quoting\nis frozen. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22119](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22119))\n\n- Rewrite an attribute value the source spelled with character\nreferences. (by\n[@&#8203;aryanraj45](https://redirect.github.com/aryanraj45) in\n[#&#8203;22110](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22110))\n\n- Unquote an HTML attribute value carrying a vertical tab. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22162](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22162))\n\n- Keep a shadow''s spread and canonicalize a merged selector list. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22101](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22101))\n\n- Leave out an implied tag and merge adjacent runs on the first pass.\n(by [@&#8203;aryanraj45](https://redirect.github.com/aryanraj45) in\n[#&#8203;22121](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22121))\n\n- Minify in one pass what a second pass of the CSS minifier used to\nfind. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22106](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22106))\n\n- Cover the CSS lookup tables no stylesheet in the corpus reaches. (by\n[@&#8203;aryanraj45](https://redirect.github.com/aryanraj45) in\n[#&#8203;22126](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22126))\n\n- Keep `initial` where an engine reads the property''s initial keyword\napart. (by [@&#8203;aryanraj45](https://redirect.github.com/aryanraj45)\nin\n[#&#8203;22128](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22128))\n\n- Join the CSS rules a cut leaves adjacent, and keep a value an escape\nate. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22108](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22108))\n\n- Drop the dead CSS a cut leaves, and join more of the blocks that print\nalike. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22111](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22111))\n\n- Run the printer equivalence suite against Firefox as well as Chrome.\n(by [@&#8203;aryanraj45](https://redirect.github.com/aryanraj45) in\n[#&#8203;22151](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22151))\n\n- Finish in one CSS pass the joins, drops and collapses left to a\nsecond. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22117](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22117))\n\n- Move the context module sources into `lib/context/`. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22115](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22115))\n\n- Declare loader context types in JSDoc instead of hand-written `.d.ts`\nfiles. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22116](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22116))\n\n- Emit a failing module''s stack relative, and name what a tap failed\nwith. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22122](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22122))\n\n- Finish in one CSS pass the drops, layer gathers and joins left to a\nsecond. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22120](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22120))\n\n- Speed up CSS parsing by stepping over dropped selector preludes in\nbytes. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22142](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22142))\n\n- Record hoisted, module and block declarations while parsing, not by\nre-walking. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22147](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22147))\n\n- Fold more enumerated attribute values and drop those naming no\nkeyword. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22148](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22148))\n\n- Halve the CSS minifier''s browser-version tables by narrowing their\nelement type. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22140](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22140))\n\n- Make each `optimization.minimize.css` switch govern its own rewrite\nalone. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22140](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22140))\n\n- Join the rules a top-level `@layer` gather leaves meeting at the seam.\n(by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22140](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22140))\n\n- Gather a CSS layer past a rule that writes only a different one. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22154](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22154))\n\n- Order HTML attributes by what reaches the output, and read values\ndecoded. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22146](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22146))\n\n- Drop a fallback declaration every `browserslist` target reads past.\n(by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22158](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22158))\n\n- Fix module library exports lost under cache or missing behind a\nre-export. (by [@&#8203;hai-x](https://redirect.github.com/hai-x) in\n[#&#8203;22114](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22114))\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Configuration\n\n📅 **Schedule**: (UTC)\n\n- Branch creation\n  - At any time (no schedule defined)\n- Automerge\n  - At any time (no schedule defined)\n\n🚦 **Automerge**: Enabled.\n\n♻ **Rebasing**: Whenever PR is behind base branch, or you tick the\nrebase/retry checkbox.\n\n🔕 **Ignore**: Close this PR and you won''t be reminded about this update\nagain.\n\n---\n\n- [ ] <!-- rebase-check -->If you want to rebase/retry this PR, check\nthis box\n\n---\n\nThis PR was generated by [Mend Renovate](https://mend.io/renovate/).\nView the [repository job\nlog](https://developer.mend.io/github/runtime-env/runtime-env).\n\n<!--renovate-debug:eyJjcmVhdGVkSW5WZXIiOiI0NC4xMDMuMCIsInVwZGF0ZWRJblZlciI6IjQ0LjEwMy4wIiwidGFyZ2V0QnJhbmNoIjoibWFpbiIsImxhYmVscyI6W119-->\n\nCo-authored-by: renovate[bot] <