8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22088](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22088))\n\n- Remove `experiments.outputModule`, set `output.module` to emit ESM\ninstead. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22011](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22011))\n\n- Add `output.copy` to copy files and directories into the output\ndirectory. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;21938](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21938))\n\n- Accept a file URL in any spelling Node reads where an absolute path is\ntaken. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22012](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22012))\n\n- Minify inline CSS and JSON via `renderEmbeddedSource`, exporting\nwebpack''s own. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;21993](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21993))\n\n- Export `cssMinify` and `htmlMinify` on `css.syntax` and `html.syntax`.\n(by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;21953](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21953))\n\n- Make `processResult` async and let a tap rename the asset it rewrote.\n(by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;21854](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21854))\n\n- Lower a CSS spelling a target cannot read and write a color fallback\nbefore one. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;21926](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21926))\n\n- Allow optional filesystem cache build dependencies. (by\n[@&#8203;xiaoxiaojx](https://redirect.github.com/xiaoxiaojx) in\n[#&#8203;21849](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21849))\n\n- Add `output.environment.topLevelAwait` and await every async ESM\nentry. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;21915](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21915))\n\n- Add `unusedSymbols` and `pseudoClasses`, and evaluate a CSS color\nfunction. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;21927](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21927))\n\n- Drop an implied shorthand slot, fold a math function, tighten color\nconversion. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;21929](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21929))\n\n- Add `module.parser.javascript.specNamespaceObject` for spec namespace\nobjects. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22049](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22049))\n\n- Drop what is already said or only a gone engine reads, add\n`lowerUnsupported`. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;21931](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21931))\n\n- Add `normalizeUrlAttributes`, `mergeScripts`, boolean and token\nswitches. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;21960](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21960))\n\n- Minify an event handler attribute, and name the production each script\nbody is. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;21968](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21968))\n\n- Add source-map, asset, module, bailout, federation hints; group config\nchecks. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;21961](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21961))\n\n- Lower CSS nesting, `:dir()` and custom at-rules; gate case folding and\nescapes. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;21950](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21950))\n\n- Add `optimization.minimize.css.mergeDistantRules` to join rules across\na gap. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;21969](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21969))\n\n##### Patch Changes\n\n- Minify an embedded body through the embedded path, dropping three html\noptions. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;21936](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21936))\n\n- Take a minified `style` attribute''s answer whatever quoting it needs.\n(by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;21936](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21936))\n\n- Name chunk imports in the chunk loader, not at each import site. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22076](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22076))\n\n- Repair hashed names; under HMR bake hashed url maps and reload moved\ncss names. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;21916](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21916))\n\n- Enable `output.module` for `module` and `modern-module` library types.\n(by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22071](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22071))\n\n- Name an anonymous `export default class` before its static\ninitializers run. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;21910](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21910))\n\n- Throw on a non-optional read past an undefined `DefinePlugin` member.\n(by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22017](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22017))\n\n- Reject a fulfilled async cycle member with the cycle''s evaluation\nerror. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;21921](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21921))\n\n- Escape external requests in generated ESM imports and star reexports.\n(by [@&#8203;bjohansebas](https://redirect.github.com/bjohansebas) in\n[#&#8203;22078](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22078))\n\n- Fix stack overflows in ESM library star reexport cycles with\nexternals. (by\n[@&#8203;bjohansebas](https://redirect.github.com/bjohansebas) in\n[#&#8203;22080](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22080))\n\n- Preserve live bindings when reexporting external ESM exports. (by\n[@&#8203;bjohansebas](https://redirect.github.com/bjohansebas) in\n[#&#8203;22082](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22082))\n\n- Use configured external requests in ESM star reexports; reject\nproperty paths. (by\n[@&#8203;bjohansebas](https://redirect.github.com/bjohansebas) in\n[#&#8203;22079](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22079))\n\n- Preserve import attributes on ESM library star reexports of externals.\n(by [@&#8203;bjohansebas](https://redirect.github.com/bjohansebas) in\n[#&#8203;22081](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22081))\n\n- Fail the build when a runtime module''s code generation throws while\nhashing. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22034](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22034))\n\n- Settle a css chunk load without a DOM where its stylesheet cannot be\nread. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;21970](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21970))\n\n- Await a deferred import''s async dependency that is evaluating-async.\n(by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;21934](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21934))\n\n- Keep a color the CSS minifier would round where its channels are read\nback. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;21923](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21923))\n\n- Refresh a cached module''s `resolveOptions` from the factory, not the\npack. (by [@&#8203;hai-x](https://redirect.github.com/hai-x) in\n[#&#8203;21945](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21945))\n\n- Read a `<script type>` decoded, so a reference-spelled type is\nminified. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;21933](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21933))\n\n- Read the extension out of a path-scoped rule''s alternation, class or\nbraces. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;21946](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21946))\n\n- Keep an HTML attribute name or list token holding a foreign template\ndelimiter. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22018](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22018))\n\n- Answer a name a module does not export from the spec namespace. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22092](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22092))\n\n- Give a deferred namespace the spec''s exotic shape when the exports are\nknown. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;21939](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21939))\n\n- Give a JSON, text or CommonJS namespace the spec''s exotic shape and\nidentity. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22087](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22087))\n\n- Report a missing asset instead of a code generation deadlock. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;21992](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21992))\n\n- Keep a concatenated CommonJS reference a separate statement, guarding\nit once. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;21962](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21962))\n\n- Keep CSS module exports for a direct loader `importModule()` call. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22047](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22047))\n\n- Fix `import.meta` and `require.main`, and scope-hoist\n`import.meta.main`. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;21973](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21973))\n\n- Honor `resolve.fileSystem` and say where `module.exprContextCritical`\nmoved. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22091](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22091))\n\n- Release stale compilation data from nested children and idle watch\nbuilds. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22096](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22096))\n\n- Resolve a `@value` once and then localize it, wherever it names an\nidentifier. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22036](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22036))\n\n- Release the printed-text store''s text when the CSS printer drops it.\n(by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;21958](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21958))\n\n- Skip a foreign dependency whose `isLazy` is a flag when walking a lazy\nbarrel. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;21998](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21998))\n\n- Move diagnostics to `buildInfo.diagnostics`, persisting parse-time\nbailouts. (by [@&#8203;hai-x](https://redirect.github.com/hai-x) in\n[#&#8203;22055](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22055))\n\n- Invalidate consumer codegen when an inlined export value changes. (by\n[@&#8203;xiaoxiaojx](https://redirect.github.com/xiaoxiaojx) in\n[#&#8203;22020](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22020))\n\n- Rebuild DelegatedModule when DLL manifest metadata changes. (by\n[@&#8203;xiaoxiaojx](https://redirect.github.com/xiaoxiaojx) in\n[#&#8203;22028](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22028))\n\n- Keep a CSS layer''s blocks in order where one of them streams. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22044](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22044))\n\n- Refuse inlining const exports across sync cycles with binding reads.\n(by [@&#8203;xiaoxiaojx](https://redirect.github.com/xiaoxiaojx) in\n[#&#8203;22085](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22085))\n\n- Escape a text run ending in `</`, which the tag after it made a\ncomment of. (by\n[@&#8203;aryanraj45](https://redirect.github.com/aryanraj45) in\n[#&#8203;22086](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22086))\n\n- Skip JS render sentinel scans on chunks without HTML. (by\n[@&#8203;xiaoxiaojx](https://redirect.github.com/xiaoxiaojx) in\n[#&#8203;21974](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21974))\n\n- Minify an attribute by what its value says, not by how the source\nspelled it. (by\n[@&#8203;aryanraj45](https://redirect.github.com/aryanraj45) in\n[#&#8203;22095](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22095))\n\n- Cut allocation and scanning in the CSS and HTML printers, output\nunchanged. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;21997](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21997))\n\n- Emit less chunk-loading runtime. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22094](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22094))\n\n- Recognize the reflected attributes of `frame`, `frameset`, `marquee`\nand `dir`. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22003](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22003))\n\n- Drop the `neo-async` dependency in favor of a faster built-in async\nhelper. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;21959](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21959))\n\n- Speed up cache serialization by cutting per-object lookups and call\nframes. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;21994](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21994))\n\n- Update dependencies and match the `ReadFileSync` type to Node.js\ntypings. (by\n[@&#8203;dependabot](https://redirect.github.com/apps/dependabot) in\n[#&#8203;21919](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21919))\n\n- Match acorn on `**` arrows, LS/PS cooking, string export names,\n`program` reuse. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;21666](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21666))\n\n- Parse a regexp literal the running engine cannot build, and keep\nlocations. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22009](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22009))\n\n- Parse without acorn, serialize parse-error locations, trim walker\nallocations. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;21667](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/21667))\n\n- Drop the `acorn` dependency in favor of webpack''s own JavaScript\nparser. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22042](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22042))\n\n- Name HTML chunks after their tags'' urls, drop the JS copy, type\n`text/html`. (by\n[@&#8203;alexander-akait](https://redirect.github.com/alexander-akait)\nin\n[#&#8203;22008](https://redirect.github.com/webpack/webpack/pull/22008))\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Configuration\n\n📅 **Schedule**: (UTC)\n\n- Branch creation\n  - At any time (no schedule defined)\n- Automerge\n  - At any time (no schedule defined)\n\n🚦 **Automerge**: Enabled.\n\n♻ **Rebasing**: Whenever PR is behind base branch, or you tick the\nrebase/retry checkbox.\n\n🔕 **Ignore**: Close this PR and you won''t be reminded about this update\nagain.\n\n---\n\n- [ ] <!-- rebase-check -->If you want to rebase/retry this PR, check\nthis box\n\n---\n\nThis PR was generated by [Mend Renovate](https://mend.io/renovate/).\nView the [repository job\nlog](https://developer.mend.io/github/runtime-env/runtime-env).\n\n<!--renovate-debug:eyJjcmVhdGVkSW5WZXIiOiI0NC43OS4xIiwidXBkYXRlZEluVmVyIjoiNDQuNzkuMSIsInRhcmdldEJyYW5jaCI6Im1haW4iLCJsYWJlbHMiOltdfQ==-->\n\nCo-authored-by: renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqp9QPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOaUQABgcaDOO/FxYK9PP7SlKSr/e\nGMZVzYn2osT9LCcQIvKIMmn55fDUMGV2H3UOadtfg7qmAf/hT1TbsEhoEaYe3Yex\nsxgKUqMTYCv4hne3Qavyc5EwBDpmPEyg3RRKNAjtpTgMNIV9XzkA98qcjtc+plHn\nO79W3+3iJKXp2CuKgOrziiPvhRhaymUafZLf1TVKb4N20YlaL9RI5S8aDd6MiNPF\n0xW6Xk04ztVUDRaPOuCqRK8tfA1QiRRAy1q2U0H0N47R0XJmXnvE/fZ59PK/4DV4\nviznyEPbjJvBqxOU6VHiycwd9JXK/IXaiGPZPmNWUaoe26eWVh90MYEG3lihL9k/\n+LPNWSHWNbNjvi7mRobfUOPNJY7AhJiNu3kECJNIH6AxJWuG8rlXfI1qG2O7KvvD\ncaNEGHFBoPNVib4K8ovye8zY01kL2X3pA7qB0p3oVIHWwKX0thUQp0Q74XOyrQyV\nYWi3fAOKm4uLRb/yO9mhAhiWBQfeT0snxkjOpRm22vije7lVOiP+rHctOKeTB3Bn\nbaAZ4HMcVA/krSC+JHzsNvud+tlvZn1Ml2pJKx3AYTnF35gLjo3xyzO6ol/6YcZg\nFfGa6o3oblu50JGaUjex8tpEtiLJJDqDuLV4PbdXd9cm3Maja6SlU/QQDh4ws/VC\n0l1sqIw5ZeVhDr/DpC